Hi Michael and Brandon,

At yesterday's lab meeting we withdrew the proposal to set staffing from the =
daily average alone. We'll keep the current intake process and reviewer assig=
nments, as recorded in MDR-CA-20241218-LR-01-R01.

The findings PDF has the day-by-day comparison. Both conditions cleared by 17=
:00 PST each day. With review paused over lunch, December 5 still had 18 revi=
ews open at 13:00 after 25 arrivals and seven completions. The item picked up=
 at restart stayed in the open count until it finished.

I've attached the 90-row comparison separately so you can check the timings b=
y intake key. In the lunch-pause columns, QD-287 shows the December 5 arrival=
 at 12:05, start at 13:00 and completion at 13:03. That's 55 minutes to start=
 and 58 minutes to finish. QD-327 is the other end of the lunch block, with t=
he last completion at 13:54.

Brandon, for the next staffing discussion let's keep the acceptable wait to s=
tart and responsibility during cover and at handback on the agenda.

Thanks,
Vanessa

